# StackScore Core Engineering Rules

StackScore is **documentation-driven software**. When docs and code conflict, treat approved documentation as authoritative until intentionally revised (see `docs/30-Architecture/DOC-129 – AI Development Rules & Engineering Constitution.md`).

## Always

- Read governing docs in `docs/` before inventing business logic, workflows, scoring, pricing, or permissions.
- Put business logic in `src/lib/**` services; keep `src/app/api/**` route handlers and UI thin.
- Reuse existing patterns before introducing new abstractions.
- Use domain language from DOC-120; StackScore is not a CRM — keep Business Profile lightweight.
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, API keys). Follow DOC-303 for RBAC.
- Only create git commits when the user explicitly asks.
- `.cursor/` maintenance updates rules and skills only — not `src/` — unless application changes are separately requested.
- Do not regress established acquisition, checkout, billing, auth, or email workflows without explicit approval.

## Architecture defaults

- **Next.js 15** App Router, **React 19**, **Node 20.x**
- **No server actions** — mutations go through `src/app/api/**` route handlers
- **Prisma 7** + PostgreSQL (Neon in production); client at `@/generated/prisma/client`, singleton at `@/lib/db`
- **Tenant boundary:** `Client` (no Organization/Workspace models)
- **Auth:** NextAuth v5 JWT; API auth per-route via `@/lib/api/helpers`
- **UI:** shadcn `base-nova` + Base UI + Tailwind v4 (CSS-first, no `tailwind.config.*`)
- **Email:** react-email templates in `src/emails/`; outbound tracking via `@/lib/communications/tracking/record-outbound`
- **PDF:** `@react-pdf/renderer` via `src/lib/pdf/generate.tsx`

## Validation before finishing

Run targeted checks for touched areas: `npm run lint`, `npm test -- <path>`, `npm run build` when risk is high.

## Load skills for detailed workflows

Use `.cursor/skills/` for task workflows (start with `repository-auditor` + the matching domain skill). Use `cursor-maintenance` to audit or refresh rules and skills.
